# Conventions for research documents

- Name files with the pattern `YYYYMMDD-underscored_name.md` (like `20260214-container_runtimes.md`)
- The date prefix signals when the research took place and sorts files chronologically
- Do not update research documents after initial publication other than linting fixes; create new research if conditions change
- Reference research documents from ADRs and design documents when they inform decisions
